1
00:00:51,946 --> 00:00:55,035
[Episode 6. Jealousy Is Yours, Revenge Is Mine]

2
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:19,205
I'm sure

3
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:24,669
you'll fall for me.

4
00:01:45,472 --> 00:01:46,524
Hey, hey, hey!

5
00:01:46,524 --> 00:01:47,817
Hey!

6
00:01:47,817 --> 00:01:48,817
Lee Eun Chae!

7
00:01:49,486 --> 00:01:51,488
What... What's with her?

8
00:01:51,488 --> 00:01:52,613
Lee Eun Chae!

9
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,607
No way.

10
00:02:32,786 --> 00:02:35,322
Did I faint?

11
00:02:35,322 --> 00:02:38,576
To be exact... you fell asleep.

12
00:02:38,576 --> 00:02:41,574
I couldn't sleep last night.

13
00:02:41,574 --> 00:02:44,388
Why? Did you catch my insomnia?

14
00:02:45,083 --> 00:02:46,209
What?

15
00:02:46,209 --> 00:02:49,212
Even the doctor said
there were no abnormalities.

16
00:02:49,212 --> 00:02:50,801
By any chance,

17
00:02:51,371 --> 00:02:54,387
was it because I was next door
and made you too nervous?

18
00:02:59,556 --> 00:03:00,693
Whatever.

19
00:03:01,725 --> 00:03:03,861
Are you making fun of me now?

20
00:03:03,861 --> 00:03:07,029
Fainting mid-kiss.

21
00:03:07,782 --> 00:03:09,393
Is that fascinating to you?

22
00:03:10,191 --> 00:03:11,348
I'm sorry.

23
00:03:12,945 --> 00:03:15,280
I didn't know you'd actually faint.

24
00:03:16,197 --> 00:03:17,197
Then...

25
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:21,553
Why did you do that to me?

26
00:03:23,496 --> 00:03:25,748
What? Do you have something to say?

27
00:03:25,748 --> 00:03:27,727
I'm not going to say anything.

28
00:03:29,252 --> 00:03:32,490
I won't tell you how I feel.

29
00:03:34,632 --> 00:03:37,176
What are you saying, Lee Eun Chae?

30
00:03:37,176 --> 00:03:39,224
Act natural.

31
00:03:39,762 --> 00:03:41,373
Instead...

32
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:54,685
I'll show you a movie.

33
00:03:55,205 --> 00:03:56,446
Why all of a sudden?

34
00:03:56,446 --> 00:04:00,040
You showed me the ocean,
so I'll show you a movie.

35
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:03,536
Are you trying to act generous
with something cheap again?

36
00:04:03,536 --> 00:04:06,664
If you put it that way,
the ocean is completely free.

37
00:04:06,664 --> 00:04:08,958
A movie costs a whole 15,000 won.

38
00:04:08,958 --> 00:04:11,127
Why don't you just ask me to show you?

39
00:04:11,127 --> 00:04:12,211
Why?

40
00:04:12,211 --> 00:04:14,549
Plan to rent out the whole theater this time?

41
00:04:14,549 --> 00:04:16,223
If you want.

42
00:04:16,223 --> 00:04:18,051
Forget it.

43
00:04:18,051 --> 00:04:19,459
Why?

44
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:23,139
Are you afraid you'll fall for me
if I spend money?

45
00:04:23,139 --> 00:04:25,400
That will never happen.

46
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:27,435
I've told you over and over.

47
00:04:27,435 --> 00:04:29,258
I'll never...

48
00:04:30,855 --> 00:04:32,493
fall for you.

49
00:04:34,474 --> 00:04:36,500
Not ever.

50
00:05:07,058 --> 00:05:12,094
I'm sure
I told you I don't listen to music like this.

51
00:05:12,647 --> 00:05:14,899
Then what kind of music do you listen to?

52
00:05:14,899 --> 00:05:16,313
Classical.

53
00:05:16,817 --> 00:05:20,572
- You're picky about music, too.
- It's my preference.

54
00:05:20,572 --> 00:05:21,756
All for show.

55
00:05:23,346 --> 00:05:26,369
Aren't you up on stage just for show, too?

56
00:05:26,369 --> 00:05:27,745
No, I'm not.

57
00:05:27,745 --> 00:05:28,745
Then why?

58
00:05:29,247 --> 00:05:31,624
Because singing makes me happy.

59
00:05:31,624 --> 00:05:36,754
And I want someone to hear my song
and be happy too.

60
00:06:01,487 --> 00:06:02,774
It's nice.

61
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:09,370
Wow! Pork belly again.

62
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:11,875
Eun Chae. It's hot. Come and eat.

63
00:06:13,499 --> 00:06:16,419
You're crazy about pork belly.
Why the long face?

64
00:06:16,419 --> 00:06:18,912
You're a mind reader. I had it yesterday.

65
00:06:18,912 --> 00:06:22,175
What kind of business trip
has you eating pork belly?

66
00:06:22,175 --> 00:06:23,466
How many went?

67
00:06:24,469 --> 00:06:26,721
Well, the whole team went.

68
00:06:26,721 --> 00:06:28,321
And how many is that?

69
00:06:29,307 --> 00:06:31,716
Eun Seo, are you interrogating me?

70
00:06:31,716 --> 00:06:33,394
It's an occupational hazard.

71
00:06:33,394 --> 00:06:37,047
I'm just suspicious because you're working
so hard at the office.

72
00:06:37,565 --> 00:06:39,776
She's not usually the hardworking type.

73
00:06:39,776 --> 00:06:42,653
My girl is getting recognized at work,

74
00:06:42,653 --> 00:06:44,570
so she got to go on the business trip.

75
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:45,573
That's right.

76
00:06:45,573 --> 00:06:48,404
That Manager Kwon went with you, right?

77
00:06:49,035 --> 00:06:50,161
Yeah.

78
00:06:50,161 --> 00:06:51,621
Manager Kwon?

79
00:06:51,621 --> 00:06:53,021
That married man?

80
00:06:54,547 --> 00:06:57,835
I'm most suspicious of that Manager Kwon.

81
00:06:57,835 --> 00:07:00,087
- He's not that kind of guy.
- Guy?

82
00:07:01,422 --> 00:07:03,341
Usually, when you talk about a boss,

83
00:07:03,341 --> 00:07:06,475
shouldn't you say "person," not "guy"?

84
00:07:06,475 --> 00:07:08,262
Bear with her.

85
00:07:08,262 --> 00:07:10,681
Your sister does this because she loves you.

86
00:07:10,681 --> 00:07:11,980
Right.

87
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,142
Look, kiddo.

88
00:07:13,142 --> 00:07:16,646
This whole mix-up is
because you don't have a boyfriend.

89
00:07:16,646 --> 00:07:17,772
- Jin Woo.
- Yes?

90
00:07:17,772 --> 00:07:20,669
What kind of person is this Dr. Moon?

91
00:07:22,068 --> 00:07:23,861
- Tae Gyeong?
- Yes.

92
00:07:23,861 --> 00:07:25,947
- He's a gem, Father.
- Really?

93
00:07:25,947 --> 00:07:29,867
Then try setting him up with Eun Chae.

94
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:31,865
What do you mean, try?

95
00:07:32,954 --> 00:07:34,413
I'll set up a blind date.

96
00:07:34,413 --> 00:07:36,249
There, happy?

97
00:07:36,999 --> 00:07:38,380
Okay, cheers.

98
00:07:39,159 --> 00:07:40,169
Seriously.

99
00:07:40,169 --> 00:07:41,169
Cheers.

100
00:07:42,338 --> 00:07:44,621
Up with it. Alright.

101
00:07:54,016 --> 00:07:57,558
The wind blows as my love for you begins.

102
00:08:06,696 --> 00:08:08,406
Why me...

103
00:08:11,993 --> 00:08:13,636
The kiss...

104
00:08:15,913 --> 00:08:17,790
A kiss is just a kiss.

105
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:19,417
Why did I have to faint?

106
00:08:20,084 --> 00:08:21,683
It's so embarrassing.

107
00:08:22,545 --> 00:08:26,230
Ugh.

108
00:08:31,637 --> 00:08:33,556
Shall I play Brahms, boss?

109
00:08:33,556 --> 00:08:37,886
I want someone to hear my song
and be happy too.

110
00:08:45,892 --> 00:08:47,910
[Pink Frankenstein]

111
00:09:33,699 --> 00:09:36,378
You should keep your promise to me.

112
00:09:41,999 --> 00:09:44,126
Why did I say I'd show him a movie?

113
00:09:44,126 --> 00:09:48,175
Why do I have to see Kwon Do Hyeok's face
on a weekend morning?

114
00:09:57,306 --> 00:09:59,641
Get a grip, Lee Eun Chae.

115
00:10:00,434 --> 00:10:03,316
You're smiling just because of one kiss.

116
00:10:03,896 --> 00:10:05,147
Seriously.

117
00:10:05,147 --> 00:10:06,899
I must be going crazy.

118
00:10:08,651 --> 00:10:10,340
I'm going to dress casual.

119
00:10:12,738 --> 00:10:14,824
I'd rather he didn't show up.

120
00:10:15,324 --> 00:10:16,894
Don't come.

121
00:10:17,368 --> 00:10:18,995
Don't come.

122
00:10:18,995 --> 00:10:20,663
Isn't that the actor Gil Jun?

123
00:10:20,663 --> 00:10:22,627
- Where?
- Gil Jun?

124
00:10:22,627 --> 00:10:24,292
Is that Gil Jun?

125
00:10:24,292 --> 00:10:26,276
No way if he is!

126
00:10:41,017 --> 00:10:43,060
What are you doing?

127
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:46,063
I thought it was chili paste, but I guess not.

128
00:10:46,063 --> 00:10:48,733
Who wears chili paste on their lips?

129
00:10:48,733 --> 00:10:52,415
Why did you suddenly put on such bold lipstick?

130
00:10:52,415 --> 00:10:54,989
My lips are none of your business.

131
00:10:54,989 --> 00:10:56,741
Do you only see my lips now?

132
00:10:56,741 --> 00:10:58,698
Yes, that's all I see.

133
00:11:00,093 --> 00:11:03,581
But it's like you want me to see them
more often.

134
00:11:03,581 --> 00:11:05,268
No, I didn't.

135
00:11:14,991 --> 00:11:17,511
That lipstick doesn't suit you.

136
00:11:17,511 --> 00:11:18,929
Don't wear it anymore.

137
00:11:18,929 --> 00:11:20,936
What's it to you?

138
00:11:20,936 --> 00:11:22,808
Just keep your mouth shut.

139
00:11:22,808 --> 00:11:27,495
You're the first woman
to tell me to keep my mouth shut.

140
00:11:29,561 --> 00:11:32,870
Why? What are you imagining now?

141
00:11:34,028 --> 00:11:35,028
Nothing.

142
00:11:37,114 --> 00:11:39,979
I'll go buy the tickets, so wait here.

143
00:11:53,124 --> 00:11:54,956
You're so handsome.

144
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:06,560
He's not Gil Jun.

145
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,938
Oh, my. Walk faster. Hurry!

146
00:12:08,938 --> 00:12:09,987
Gosh.

147
00:12:12,525 --> 00:12:14,526
Who's Gil Jun?

148
00:12:15,035 --> 00:12:17,870
There's this guy. A movie star.

149
00:12:17,870 --> 00:12:20,104
A very handsome one, too.

150
00:12:20,783 --> 00:12:22,303
How unpleasant.

151
00:12:23,536 --> 00:12:27,039
Take off those sunglasses
if you don't want to be mistaken for him.

152
00:12:27,039 --> 00:12:29,403
You don't look like him without them.

153
00:12:33,295 --> 00:12:34,549
Is that so?

154
00:12:38,935 --> 00:12:43,338
Maybe he's even more handsome than Gil Jun.

155
00:12:45,307 --> 00:12:47,059
Handsome, my foot.

156
00:12:47,059 --> 00:12:48,963
He just looks mean.

157
00:12:51,564 --> 00:12:53,855
You've been to a movie theater, right?

158
00:12:54,483 --> 00:12:56,276
No.

159
00:12:56,276 --> 00:12:59,029
You really do live in a different world.

160
00:12:59,029 --> 00:13:01,147
What have you been doing with your life?

161
00:13:01,147 --> 00:13:04,323
Mostly things you couldn't do.

162
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:08,893
By the way,

163
00:13:08,893 --> 00:13:13,065
what were you getting treated for
when you went to see Jin Woo?

164
00:13:18,007 --> 00:13:20,979
Why should I tell you that?

165
00:13:56,313 --> 00:13:57,862
Well, then.

166
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:00,399
Let's go our separate ways now.

167
00:14:04,753 --> 00:14:08,140
For someone who's so strict about meal times,

168
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:09,552
aren't you hungry?

169
00:14:10,351 --> 00:14:12,645
- No, I'm not.
- Well, I am.

170
00:14:12,645 --> 00:14:14,073
Let's go eat.

171
00:14:19,506 --> 00:14:21,946
Oh, Eun Chae. It is you!

172
00:14:21,946 --> 00:14:24,281
Woo Su Mi. Hello.

173
00:14:24,281 --> 00:14:25,699
Have you been well?

174
00:14:25,699 --> 00:14:26,901
Yes.

175
00:14:28,210 --> 00:14:30,371
I see you're here with your brother.

176
00:14:30,371 --> 00:14:32,122
My brother?

177
00:14:32,122 --> 00:14:35,399
Hello. You remember me, right?

178
00:14:38,087 --> 00:14:41,516
He said he was your brother. He asked for help.

179
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,594
He said even the smallest detail would help.

180
00:14:48,403 --> 00:14:51,828
But why is your brother so handsome?

181
00:14:51,828 --> 00:14:52,893
Maybe that's why.

182
00:14:52,893 --> 00:14:56,071
Everyone told him everything
they saw and heard.

183
00:14:56,689 --> 00:14:59,541
By the way, Eun Chae,
about those hallway cameras.

184
00:14:59,541 --> 00:15:02,027
Did you know
they cover the conference room too?

185
00:15:02,027 --> 00:15:03,390
Really?

186
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:07,366
Evidence was clear. What could the manager do?

187
00:15:07,366 --> 00:15:09,515
I heard he begged for mercy.

188
00:15:10,135 --> 00:15:14,156
Your brother even gave me
these earrings to thank me.

189
00:15:15,874 --> 00:15:17,918
Oh, right. I'm meeting a friend.

190
00:15:17,918 --> 00:15:20,643
- I should get going.
- Sure.

191
00:15:20,643 --> 00:15:22,756
Take care, Eun Chae. I'll call you.

192
00:15:22,756 --> 00:15:23,756
Okay.

193
00:15:40,733 --> 00:15:43,390
Why were you digging into my past?

194
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:49,158
Well... It's not that...

195
00:15:49,158 --> 00:15:51,007
So, was it fun?

196
00:15:51,577 --> 00:15:56,165
I was sexually harassed
and got kicked out like an idiot.

197
00:15:56,165 --> 00:15:58,828
But you solved it so easily.

198
00:16:00,836 --> 00:16:02,438
Was it entertaining?

199
00:16:32,576 --> 00:16:34,203
Welcome.

200
00:16:41,335 --> 00:16:43,570
Only the expensive ones are left.

201
00:16:48,842 --> 00:16:52,086
I think I can run to the bus stop.

202
00:16:52,888 --> 00:16:54,555
Gosh.

203
00:17:15,786 --> 00:17:17,126
Take this.

204
00:18:02,950 --> 00:18:05,062
I should be the one mad here.

205
00:18:29,777 --> 00:18:32,343
Is she still angry?

206
00:18:37,868 --> 00:18:39,250
This way.

207
00:18:42,956 --> 00:18:44,249
Please say hello.

208
00:18:44,249 --> 00:18:47,784
This is Jeong Mi Seon,
former CEO of OYES Entertainment.

209
00:18:47,784 --> 00:18:50,297
Hello.

210
00:18:51,365 --> 00:18:52,820
Do Hyeok's secretary?

211
00:18:53,801 --> 00:18:54,989
Yes.

212
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:59,097
I'm Do Hyeok's mother.

213
00:18:59,097 --> 00:19:01,351
I see.

214
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,898
What brings you here unannounced?

215
00:19:08,315 --> 00:19:10,226
You do know that...

216
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:13,442
I founded this company.

217
00:19:13,442 --> 00:19:15,113
But tell me,

218
00:19:15,113 --> 00:19:18,575
how could you decide
to drop an artist all by yourself?

219
00:19:18,575 --> 00:19:21,411
Even if your father made you the CEO,

220
00:19:21,411 --> 00:19:23,622
shouldn't you have told me, the owner?

221
00:19:23,622 --> 00:19:26,151
As far as I know, after continued deficits,

222
00:19:26,151 --> 00:19:28,634
the company was acquired by Seheon Group.

223
00:19:28,634 --> 00:19:32,023
I believe you are currently
an in-house director.

224
00:19:34,130 --> 00:19:36,468
You're as precise as ever.

225
00:19:36,468 --> 00:19:37,468
Yes.

226
00:19:39,024 --> 00:19:41,890
Even if you don't know the industry,

227
00:19:41,890 --> 00:19:44,518
how could you make such a decision
so arbitrarily?

228
00:19:44,518 --> 00:19:46,562
Human error.

229
00:19:46,562 --> 00:19:49,731
If a problem repeats, you have to re-code it.

230
00:19:49,731 --> 00:19:51,024
Coding?

231
00:19:51,024 --> 00:19:53,569
I heard you built some computer room.

232
00:19:53,569 --> 00:19:55,779
Were you going to keep quiet about that too?

233
00:19:55,779 --> 00:19:57,197
Hear it from Father.

234
00:19:57,197 --> 00:19:59,616
Your father wouldn't tell me...

235
00:20:03,161 --> 00:20:04,496
Fine.

236
00:20:04,496 --> 00:20:07,124
Drop the artist if that's what you want.

237
00:20:07,124 --> 00:20:08,417
In return,

238
00:20:08,417 --> 00:20:11,492
you'd better report what you're doing to me.

239
00:20:12,754 --> 00:20:13,929
Yes.

240
00:20:17,384 --> 00:20:18,468
Please leave now.

241
00:20:18,468 --> 00:20:20,297
I have a lot to do.

242
00:20:24,030 --> 00:20:28,898
Anyway, you'd better not go behind my back.

243
00:21:23,417 --> 00:21:26,203
Did you want to touch me?

244
00:21:29,373 --> 00:21:31,265
You have a fever.

245
00:21:36,296 --> 00:21:38,664
I think you have a cold.

246
00:21:41,168 --> 00:21:43,086
It's just a cold.

247
00:21:46,098 --> 00:21:47,570
Hold on.

248
00:22:04,116 --> 00:22:07,411
At least I won't drop dead
in the street somewhere.

249
00:22:07,411 --> 00:22:09,454
You still have the energy to joke.

250
00:22:09,454 --> 00:22:10,747
I mean,

251
00:22:10,747 --> 00:22:12,926
who told you to walk in the rain?

252
00:22:15,450 --> 00:22:18,609
Whose fault do you think that is?

253
00:22:33,478 --> 00:22:34,953
About yesterday,

254
00:22:35,647 --> 00:22:37,482
I'm sorry.

255
00:22:37,482 --> 00:22:40,406
I'll pay you back later.

256
00:22:42,122 --> 00:22:44,390
Money won't be enough.

257
00:22:46,913 --> 00:22:49,828
Whatever it is,
even you'll have a day when you need me.

258
00:22:49,828 --> 00:22:51,289
Some day.

259
00:23:08,589 --> 00:23:09,625
[Dr. Moon Tae Gyeong]

260
00:23:20,817 --> 00:23:22,277
Hello?

261
00:23:22,277 --> 00:23:24,196
Hi, it's Moon Tae Gyeong.

262
00:23:24,196 --> 00:23:25,914
Yes, hello.

263
00:23:26,406 --> 00:23:29,367
Eun Chae, I have a favor to ask.

264
00:23:29,367 --> 00:23:31,078
A favor?

265
00:23:31,078 --> 00:23:32,204
What is it?

266
00:23:32,204 --> 00:23:37,250
This weekend, our hospital is holding
a charity event for children with cancer.

267
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:41,172
I was wondering
if you could perform a song for us.

268
00:23:42,089 --> 00:23:44,132
I'd love to.

269
00:23:44,132 --> 00:23:48,011
But since it's a charity event, there's no pay.

270
00:23:48,011 --> 00:23:50,711
That's fine.

271
00:23:51,264 --> 00:23:53,350
That's not important at all.

272
00:23:53,350 --> 00:23:55,632
I'll bring all my band members.

273
00:23:57,375 --> 00:23:59,322
[Azen Tower]

274
00:24:16,656 --> 00:24:19,575
